    "edge_media_to_caption": {
        "edges": [
            {
                "node": {
                    "created_at": "1776971903",
                    "text": "An area of interest I’ve been exploring for some time now: diet as a source of bioactive peptides and their effects on overall health and well-being throughout life.\n\nHighly underfunded and understudied concept.\n\nLittle is known about the quantities, bioavailability, and bio activity of the peptides from foods, but I believe the potential is immense.\n\nNose to tail eating and diets rich in fermented foods built some of the most robust groups of people throughout time, and I theorize peptides through foods played a role in their health, resilience, and physical excellence.\n\nNew article introducing my exploration of this topic released today. You can comment “peptide article” if you want the link sent to your DMs :)",
                    "id": "18118189951598467"
                }
            }
        ]
    },
